# REPLAN 2026-11-02. Overrides the decisions below where they differ:
#   - The goal: the copilot first, voice as a rapid follow on the hardware I have.
#   - The copilot's done test: p95 under 15 s with 0 cycles lost, on a replay under normal load. It
#     replaces 2.5 s, which came from a spoken reply. The copilot does not stream and cycles at most
#     every 25 s. Evidence so far is one quiet session: 11 of 11 ok, mean 8.2 s, none over 15 s.
#   - The copilot names Flash, thinking off. Steps 4 and 5 no longer apply to it. If the replay
#     fails on Flash, the next lever is the copilot on pve's model, if that model passes the 11 bar cases.
#   - Voice keeps a fast target on its own path: 2.5 s total for the LLM part. First slice:
#     push-to-talk, spoken by Android and macOS on-device TTS. No Kokoro, no GPU for TTS.
#   - pve's 2070 runs one larger model, alias interactive, up to the card's 7 GiB.
#   - Whisper stays on the gaming PC. Rule change: Live MAY depend on it. Gaming means I don't need
#     Live. When it is away, Live says so, keeps the audio, and transcribes later. No page.
#   - So ollama stays at 0, GPU moves 1 to 3 are cancelled, and fast-chat keeps its heavy fallback.
#   - Jev goes to the gaming PC's CPU. The card holds one pod and Whisper has it. Rule change for
#     that pod only: it may run there because jev-cpu stays as its fallback off that node. pi-durable
#     keeps running while I game, so the guard must not depend on the PC alone. It still fails closed.
#   - 12 step 6 is cancelled: ollama is not coming back. Task 12's DONE WHEN is R1's test.
#   - Task 15's premise changes: speech is the gaming PC, TTS is on-device for the first slice.

# DECIDED 2026-11-01, starting from docs/plans/fast-tier.md's recommendations:
#   - Reserved path (decision 10): a separate small model on pve, alias interactive, falling back to
#     heavy. Which model stays provisional: steps 4 and 5 run only if 12 step 3 agrees, and the 3B
#     has to pass the copilot evals. If it fails, the next option is a small model on the Spark.
#     Result 2026-11-02: the 3B failed (#254, rechecked #257). 3b looks for a reply and model that pass.
#   - voice_timeout_s (decision 6): keep 30 s. fast-chat and fast-coder get timeout 5, no retries,
#     and ollama does not return before that lands.
#   - Task 12's done test: copilot total p95 under 2.5 s on a replay. Set slo_copilot_roundtrip_p95_s
#     to match once it is met.
#   - The best-effort tier alert window: 12 hours. It stays, because ollama comes back (below).
#   - The gaming PC runs Kubernetes workloads unless I am gaming, so it stays best-effort and nothing
#     may depend on it. The pve move to jev on 2026-10-22 was not deliberate.
#   - pve runs Whisper plus the interactive model, a new profile at 4 + 3 = 7 of 7 GiB. Speech and Jev
#     are both important but need not run at once. Jev stays on jev-cpu, slower but still guarding,
#     and can return to the GPU by a profile switch when no session needs it.
#   - Task 11 closes on the interactive route: the SLO is met through the gateway, on the route
#     interactive callers use, not on Flash.
#   - I own LiteLLM upgrades (decision 9). 22 proposes the trigger and cadence.

# GPU moves 1 to 3: CANCELLED by the replan. R4 and R5 replace them. Checked 2026-11-02 21:35 UTC: pve
