# R1b. Depends on: a weekday with agents busy, on the load gate in fast-tier.md. Held by the clock.
# R1's first replay failed the load gate on an idle engine: p95 14.75 s, 0 of 24 lost, 0 of 24 cycles
# saw a queue. So the done test is open, and R1's session expected it to fail under load.
#chore/copilot-replay-busy @forge: This is R1b of the REPLAN in Tasks.herd. Work in Operate mode. You're working in lordmuffin/jarvis-voice. Read the REPLAN, The replay, The done test and What to watch on lab in docs/plans/fast-tier.md, and jarvis_live/replay.py. Goal: finish R1's done test, which its first replay left open because the engine was idle. Scope: a) Before starting, read Flash's metrics. Start only when the engine is busy enough to meet the load gate. If it is not, wait and check again, and say so if the day ends without it. Never add load to make the gate pass. b) Replay against lab at real-time speed, the same way as the first run, and record the load period as Task 11 requires. c) Report p50, p95 by nearest rank, cycles lost, retries and JSON failures, and every row of What to watch on lab. d) If a release has moved lab on, say what changed from the first run. Constraints: no Flash serving args, no cluster or homelab changes, no setting changed. If the run fails the load gate, it does not count, whatever its p95. This repo is public. One PR, titled docs(plans), left for me to merge. DONE WHEN: on a run that passes the load gate, fast-tier.md says whether p95 is under 15 s with 0 cycles lost, and if not, that the next lever is the copilot on R5's model.

