#chore/interactive-model-eval @forge: This is R2 of the REPLAN in Tasks.herd. Work in Operate mode. You're working in lordmuffin/jarvis-voice. Read the REPLAN, docs/plans/fast-tier.md, server/src/jarvis_live/voice/service.py, voice/schema.py, server/tests/evals/ and chore/copilot-reply-size's reply_size.py and write-up. Goal: choose the model for pve's 2070 now it has the whole card: 7 GiB, Whisper elsewhere. Scope: a) No voice eval exists. Build one in eval-only code from invented transcripts, on the real VOICE_SYSTEM and VoiceRequest, thinking off, and state its pass bar before running anything. b) At most 3 candidates that fit 7 GiB with their context and slots, by the plan's evidence, not vendor benchmarks. Say what speed the 2070 should give each and how that is known, and name it unproven if it is an estimate. c) Run each on the voice eval, and on the 17 copilot cases at three runs each, because the copilot falls back to this model if Flash fails the replay. Report the 11 bar cases, tokens per reply and whether voice fits 2.5 s on that card. Stop a candidate once it cannot pass voice. d) If any template ignores enable_thinking, turn reasoning off at the server before judging it: lfm25-26b's first runs measured reasoning, not the reply. Constraints: all inference local on CPU, images by digest, models by SHA256, self-hosted weights only, no Flash, no gateway, no pods. Eval-only code, defaulting to today's requests. This repo is public. One PR, titled chore(plans), left for me to merge. DONE WHEN: the plan names the model and what I still have to decide, from measurements.

# R4. DONE 2026-11-03: drills passed (88 of 88 guard calls ok, worst 6.7 s), PR 3 (homelab #848) freed
# pve's card, and #850-#852 fixed the severity bug, so JevUnavailable cleared. The systemctl suspend,
