# Talking during a stream. Commented out: its plan is PR #310, waiting for my approval. Do not restart it.
# Hold-to-ask needs a client that sends the hold and speaks the reply. An OBS stream is audio in
# only, so today nothing can ask or hear an answer during one.
#docs/stream-talkback @forge: Work in Build mode and follow TDD.md, but write docs/plans/stream-talkback.md and STOP for approval before any code. You're working in lordmuffin/jarvis-voice. Read docs/plans/voice-push-to-talk.md, docs/obs.md, server/src/jarvis_live/streams/, server/src/jarvis_live/voice/ (desk.py, ask.py, ask_pass.py), protocol/v1/ (ask_begin, ask_end, ask_reply, ask_played, tickets and roles), and the hold-to-ask paths in the macOS app and Android. Goal: while I stream or record through OBS into a live session, I hold a key, ask a question, and hear a short answer in my headphones, as hold-to-ask does on the Fold and the Mac. Scope: a) Compare at least: the Mac app (or the Fold) joining the stream's session as a companion that sends only the hold markers and plays the reply; the companion sending its own mic for the ask only; and an OBS hotkey through obs-websocket. Recommend one. b) The clock: the hold's t_ms must line up with the stream's audio, which arrives through MediaMTX and ffmpeg with its own delay, and resets the timeline after a drop. Say how the server maps one to the other, and how a test proves it. c) Keep Jarvis out of the stream: the reply is spoken only into headphones, and must never reach OBS's desktop audio, the recording, the viewers or the transcript. Say how each option guarantees that, and what the echo guard does if it fails. d) Joining: how the companion finds the stream's session and gets a ticket without a device token going into OBS, and what happens when the stream ends or another stream starts. e) Meeting-silent, local-only and restricted keep their hold-to-ask rules. f) A TDD order and one PR per phase, each shippable alone. Constraints: protocol changes need fixtures and server and Swift tests in the same PR. Instrument components only. Lab only. This repo is public: no stream keys, hosts or addresses. Close with my open questions. DONE WHEN: docs/plans/stream-talkback.md is in a docs(plans) PR and you have stopped for my approval.

