# 2026-11-03: the 03:00 UTC live backup sat in ContainerCreating on agent-a for an hour. Its affinity
# picked eligible nodes but not the app's, and it mounts two ReadWriteOnce claims the app holds.
# A manual run pinned to the app's node finished at 04:24:59 UTC, and /healthz reports it fresh.
# #281 adds podAffinity to the app's pods, and a combined policy that denies the old shape.
# Live's CronJob carries the podAffinity since 0.34.1. The manual job and three failed vault-clone
# jobs from 5 and 13 days ago were deleted. The first scheduled run with the fix is 2026-11-04 03:00.

# Task 21: ALERTS THAT FIRE WHEN THE ENGINE FREEZES (priority: high)
# PLAN APPROVED 2026-11-01, STEPS 1a TO 2 AND #264 MERGED. THE REST IS READY, as feat/llm-path-alerts-rest.
# Session feat-llm-path-alerts-build is gone, last active 2026-11-02 23:00 UTC, so nothing owns it.
# Step 2 is live, the vllm-heavy PodMonitor. Nothing in Grafana has been seen rendered yet.
# Step 5 must not use le="1": Prometheus 3.14 stored le="1.0", so the plan's check reads empty, and
# empty can look like a pass. Use le="1.0" or a regex for both. Step 5's hold on
# chore/fast-tier-comparison has cleared (#254).
# agent-a is not settled: 5 watched containers restarted 19:15 to 19:31 UTC, and Prometheus stayed up
# through that. The lead is the pve2 host, unproven, not CI. The page path still sits on that node.
# 2026-11-03 04:10 UTC: agent-a at 74% CPU, most of it short-lived Forgejo runner jobs, with runner
# pods exiting in Error. Its democratic-csi node plugin failed liveness probes (15 s timeouts) and
# had restarted 37 times. Lab's image pull took 4m43s there; live's, on agent-d, did not stall.
# The node reported no pressure. Kubelet and containerd logs were not read: that needs node access.
# Homelab main's validate was failing, cause unknown, and #845's result was never rechecked.
# The mimir and grafana HelmReleases are Failed, from 2026-10-13 and 10-15, before this work, so
