90 characters per reply and eats a small max_tokens budget. complete_json defaults to think=True and only the finalizer sets it, so the copilot and voice (voice/service.py) send thinking on today. Fix that for live callers, test whether voice with no chat_template_kwargs actually reasons on Flash, and confirm the setting survives LiteLLM's drop_params. - Recommend the reserved path for interactive callers (Task 11 steps 5 and 6) now, not after Task 11 step 3. Under normal load (#239) the largest wait is the queue for a place on the engine: 7.4 of 8 in use, requests waiting in 90% of samples, and a smaller chunk does not give a queued request a place. It stays behind the gateway and is not the direct-to-vLLM bypass, which I dropped. Compare at least: a concurrency cap in pi-durable, a per-alias parallel request cap in LiteLLM, which would need no Flash restart, and a separate small model. A read of docs/pi-durable.md, its StatefulSet and apps/ai/litellm-proxy.yaml on 2026-11-01 found no such limit today; confirm that. Whether LiteLLM 1.104.2 can cap aliases that share a backend is unverified. KV cache sat above 90% in 59% of samples, so say whether a free place alone is enough, and what the cap costs agents. - Alert when a best-effort tier has been down longer than a set window. - Correct the fast-chat latency assumption in the talkback design. Constraints: the gaming PC stays best-effort, nothing may depend on it being up. DONE WHEN: copilot total p95 is under 2.5 s on a replayed session, decided 2026-11-01 because the copilot does not stream, and a downed tier raises exactly one alert.

