#fix/llm-probe-guards @forge: This is the follow-up to the review of #254 (Task 12 step 3 in Tasks.herd). Work in Build mode and follow TDD.md. You're working in lordmuffin/jarvis-voice. Read scripts/llm_probe.py, server/tests/test_llm_probe.py, server/tests/evals/transcripts.py, server/tests/evals/harness.py and the comparison section of docs/plans/fast-tier.md. Goal: the probe can't run unguarded against a model that guards pi-durable's bash, and the numbers behind "the 3B fails, step 4 stops" are rechecked. Fix these five, each with a test that fails first: 1) SlotGuard._loop (about line 1174) catches only OSError and ValueError, so http.client.IncompleteRead or a malformed slot entry kills the daemon thread silently and the run continues unprotected. Make the guard fail closed, the way post_once treats HTTPException, and stop the run. 2) SlotGuard (about line 1164) counts the probe's own request as busy, so it false-trips on the --parallel 1 pod that fast-tier.md specifies for step 4: note(1, 1) returns True on the third poll. Allow for the probe's own request, as load_bucket does, and keep a real queue tripping it. 3) The guard watches slots only, but the jev-llm OOM on 2026-11-01 came from memory growth of about 45 MiB per request. Add a stop condition for memory or restarts, and correct the docstring near line 38, which still presents the guard and the same recipe as the safety measure. Step 4 needs RSS tracked. If it can't be read without new access or a new dependency, stop and say so instead of adding either. 4) copilot_report (about line 1649) gates on all rows, but direct rows go to a different engine from the sampled Flash metrics, which dilutes queued and miscounts alone. Gate on gateway rows only, and leave voice_report as it is. Recompute the 1.2% and 14.8% in fast-tier.md from the stored rows and say whether any gate result changes. 5) In transcripts.py (about line 113) the Priya action in PLANNING_FIRST and PLANNING_LONG matches on the bare word lakeside, so find_action can return another owner's action and fail a correct reply. Tighten it, and tighten the rolling key's loose word unit. Check both models' 0 of 3 on those cases by regrading stored replies if the rows hold them, and say plainly if they don't. Then state in fast-tier.md whether the 3B verdict and step 4's stop still stand. Stored rows are in /tmp/claude-1000/-home-lordmuffin-git-wt-jarvis-voice-chore-fast-tier-comparison/3fff9031-7ad6-41aa-8f18-bf5208a74903/scratchpad/, in cop/ and ev/. Read them, never commit them: this repo is public. Constraints: no inference at all, no probe runs, no cluster or homelab changes, so anything that needs a live rerun is named as outstanding, not run. Leave the other review findings alone. Step 3a, the required CopilotDelta keys, and step 3b are out of scope. One PR, title scoped to what it fixes, and leave it for me to merge. DONE WHEN: the PR is open with its tests passing, and fast-tier.md says from the stored rows whether the gate figures and the 3B verdict change.

