straints: no other inference, no probe runs against any pod, no cluster or homelab changes, do not touch the Flash serving args, and no protocol/ change, since CopilotDelta is LLM output and not the wire format. If you find it does touch the wire format, stop and say so. Reply size and shorter replies are step 3b, out of scope: required keys may make replies longer, so report tokens per reply before and after if the evals record them. Findings 6 to 11 of the #254 review stay out of scope. This repo is public: nothing private in fixtures. Title it fix(server), because it changes what live sends and should release. One PR, left for me to merge. It goes to lab on merge and needs a lab soak before release: the release PR (#258 today) promotes to live, so say in the PR not to merge the release PR until the soak passes. DONE WHEN: the PR is open with tests passing and the live eval result reported.

